---
import { getImage } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Lightbox from '../components/Lightbox.astro';
import { site } from '../site';
import birds from '../assets/totoro-momo.jpeg';

const birdsFull = await getImage({ src: birds, width: 1086, format: 'webp' });
---

<Base variant="home">
  <div class="bio">
    <p>
      Hello, World! I’m a mechanical engineer by degree, biomedical engineer by PhD, and these days
      mostly AI and cloud-native by trade. Honestly, the lines between them keep getting thinner,
      and I like it that way :-)
    </p>
    <p>
      In a nutshell, I like tinkering with tech: from streaming a heartbeat off a digital
      stethoscope to a doctor in another city, to wiring the latest language model into an
      enterprise app, with the odd silly Python script in between. Jack of all trades, master of
      some, and the trades keep changing.
    </p>
    <p>
      Right now I lead AI and innovation at{' '}
      <a class="accent" href={site.employer.url} rel="noopener" target="_blank">{site.employer.name}</a>,
      where I build AI tools for enterprise clients, run the cloud infrastructure behind them, and
      help the team decide what’s worth building next.
    </p>
    <p>
      Before that, I worked with the Department of Biomedical Physics & Technology at Dhaka
      University and Bibeat Ltd. on affordable healthcare for low- and middle-income countries. I
      led software for homegrown medical devices and helped build a telemedicine platform that has
      been recognised internationally.
    </p>
    <p>
      When I’m not coding, I’m usually reading, tech blogs by day and paperbacks by night, planning
      trips with a roughly twenty-five percent departure rate, or playing peekaboo with my pet
      birds,{' '}
      <a class="accent" href={birdsFull.src} data-lightbox data-alt="Totoro and Momo">Totoro and Momo</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>

<Lightbox />

<style>
  .bio {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 18px;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .accent {
    text-decoration-color: var(--accent);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .bio {
      gap: 16px;
    }
  }
</style>
